{"hash":"187e22f3d69d2f42","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":84.076,"said":"You are in the hall now, its pillars running ahead of you toward the sanctum. Picture Daruka storming into the prison. ‘Merchant, what are you meditating on? Tell me the truth, and you will live.’ Supriya answered quietly, ‘I do not know.’ Daruka was enraged, and ordered his rakshasas to kill him. They rushed in with their weapons raised. Frightened, Supriya did the one thing he knew how to do: he called out. ‘O Shiva, save me. Lord of the three worlds, you alone are all I have. I belong to you.’ And the Purana says that Shiva rose up out of a cleft in the ground, with a shining temple of four doors, and stood within it in his radiant form. Supriya worshipped him right there in the prison, and Shiva gave him the Pashupata, his own invincible weapon. In a moment Daruka and his whole army were gone. Then Shiva blessed the forest itself, that good people and sages would live in it once more. But one person was left behind, grieving: Daruki. Walk on toward Nandi, who sits gazing toward the steps that go down to the sanctum.\n\nDid you know? The Pashupata is Shiva’s own weapon; in the Mahabharata, Arjuna wins it from Shiva after his penance in the Himalaya.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1035},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1051,"end":1168}],"words":[[0.098,0.204,0,3],[0.314,0.18,4,7],[0.507,0.096,8,10],[0.615,0.096,11,14],[0.723,0.276,15,19],[1.012,0.349,20,23],[1.552,0.192,25,28],[1.757,0.469,29,36],[2.237,0.373,37,44],[2.622,0.204,45,50],[2.838,0.192,51,53],[3.043,0.144,54,57],[3.199,0.337,58,64],[3.548,0.096,65,68],[3.656,0.637,69,76],[5.216,0.397,78,85],[5.625,0.433,86,92],[6.07,0.565,93,101],[6.647,0.228,102,106],[6.887,0.072,107,110],[6.971,0.529,111,117],[8.389,0.577,120,128],[9.147,0.228,130,134],[9.387,0.108,135,138],[9.507,0.072,139,142],[9.591,0.589,143,153],[10.192,0.312,154,156],[11.418,0.204,158,162],[11.635,0.12,163,165],[11.767,0.096,166,169],[11.